Moves didn't happen even after spectator off. Why? `game.paused` might still be true from initial spectator start; toggleSpectator calls resumeGameClock, which does:
```js
if (!game.clocks || !game.started || game.over || !game.paused) return;
game.paused=false...
```
game.started=false, so it returns without clearing `game.paused`. Then `canInteract` returns false due to paused true. Bug! When game starts in spectator mode, `game.paused=true` but game.started=false, and toggling spectator off calls resumeGameClock which early-returns because not started, leaving paused true. Need fix resumeGameClock: if !game.started, still clear paused? The clock shouldn't start until first move, but paused flag should clear. Modify:
```js
function resumeGameClock(){
 if(!game.clocks||game.over||!game.paused) return;
 game.paused=false;
 if(game.started) game.lastTick=performance.now();
}
```
Also pauseGameClock if !started currently returns without setting paused when spectator toggled on before start. In toggleSpectator, if game.spectator true and game.started false, pauseGameClock returns; but `game.paused` remains false. Yet game.spectator itself blocks input, so okay. But when started in spectator from setup, game.paused true. resume should clear regardless of started. Fix.

Also `canInteract` blocks if game.paused; after startup spectator and resume, cleared. Good.

Let's fix.

